# Vanessa Security Warning Handling Policy

> RULES — mandatory requirements for interpreting launch blocks via `Предупреждение безопасности`.

## MUST

| Requirement | Description |
|------------|-------------|
| Event log entry as trigger | If the event log has an entry about `Предупреждение безопасности`, the agent MUST treat it as a trigger for visual verification |
| Visual verification is mandatory | After such a signal, the agent MUST use a real screen: noVNC or a screenshot |
| Do not rely on X11 heuristics | Do not draw conclusions based solely on `wmctrl`/`xwininfo`/window titles |
| Trust-flow only for the first run | The first launch after changing the EPF is not considered a valid test run |

The detailed procedure is described in the diagnostics and GUI skills.

